    "md5": "2f516a5c810b7849e5f06451261bc0e6",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 901,
    "chunk_text": "Mahanayake Thera says President has not responded to letter on judges\u2019 retirement age\n\nColombo, Aug. 12 (Daily Mirror) - Malwatta Chapter Mahanayake Thera Most Venerable Thibbatuwawe Sri Sumangala Thera said President Anura Kumara Dissanayake had yet to respond to a letter sent by the Mahanayake Theras concerning the proposed extension of the retirement age of judges.\n\nSpeaking during a meeting with representatives of a human rights organisation in Kandy, the Mahanayake Thera said the Maha Sangha had, since ancient times, provided rulers with advice on matters of national importance, both verbally and in writing.\n\nHe said that, in previous instances, the authorities had at least acknowledged receipt of letters sent by the Mahanayake Theras.\n\n\u201cOn this matter, however, we have not received a reply so far. We have not even been informed whether the letter was received,\u201d the Thera said."
