    "chunk_text": "BASL urges President to consult experts before extending judges\u2019 retirement age\n\nColombo, Aug. 12 (Daily Mirror) - The Bar Association of Sri Lanka (BASL) has urged President Anura Kumara Dissanayake to make a decision on the proposed constitutional amendment to extend the retirement age of judges only after conducting a broad consultation with experts, BASL President Rajeev Amarasuriya said.\n\nSpeaking to the media following a meeting with the President at the Presidential Secretariat today (12), Amarasuriya said the discussion had been successful and expressed hope that it would lead to a change in the government\u2019s position on the proposed amendment.\n\n\u201cWe discussed our position with the President. This was the first time we met the President regarding this matter. We had requested a meeting some time ago,\u201d Amarasuriya said.\n\nHe said the BASL had explained why serving judges opposed the proposed constitutional amendment.\n\n\u201cWe clearly explained why the professional judges are opposed to this constitutional amendment. More than 20 people participated in the discussion, including President\u2019s Counsels, former presidents of the Bar Association and professors,\u201d he said.\n\nAmarasuriya said the BASL had requested that the proposed amendment be considered after a comprehensive discussion with relevant experts."
