    "md5": "5d7029650a121e404b135fdf526716df",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1931,
    "chunk_text": "President says judges\u2019 retirement age extension not aimed at any individual\n\nColombo, Aug. 12 (Daily Mirror) - President Anura Kumara Dissanayake has stressed that the decision to extend the retirement age of judges was not taken with any individual or group in mind, but in the broader public interest.\n\nThe President made the remarks during a meeting with representatives of the Bar Association of Sri Lanka (BASL) at the Presidential Secretariat today (12), where the proposed 22nd Amendment to the Constitution concerning the retirement age of judges was discussed.\n\nThe meeting, which lasted nearly an hour, saw BASL representatives present their views and recommendations on the proposed amendment. The President listened to their concerns and outlined the Government\u2019s position, as well as plans to strengthen and improve the country\u2019s judicial system.\n\nPresident Dissanayake said the administration of justice did not rest solely with the judiciary, but was an integrated process involving investigations, prosecutions and adjudication.\n\nHe said the Government was taking steps to strengthen the human resources of the Attorney General\u2019s Department, the Commission to Investigate Allegations of Bribery or Corruption (CIABOC), the Sri Lanka Police and the Government Analyst\u2019s Department.\n\nPlans are also underway to expand CIABOC services to the district level, increase the number of Court of Appeal judges and provide infrastructure to enable the Court of Appeal to conduct proceedings regionally, with the aim of making access to justice more convenient for the public, he said.\n\nThe President also highlighted plans to increase the number of High Court judges and improve the physical infrastructure and facilities of courts.\n\nHe stressed that the proposed extension of judges\u2019 retirement age was only one component of a broader reform programme aimed at addressing issues across the entire justice system."
  },
