    "chunk_size_bytes": 829,
    "chunk_text": "The President also highlighted plans to increase the number of High Court judges and improve the physical infrastructure and facilities of courts.\n\nHe stressed that the proposed extension of judges\u2019 retirement age was only one component of a broader reform programme aimed at addressing issues across the entire justice system.\n\nBASL representatives said they had no policy objection to increasing the number of judges or extending the retirement age of judges. However, they proposed that the decision to extend the retirement age be reconsidered with a view to reaching a broader consensus.\n\nMinister of Justice and National Integration Harshana Nanayakkara, President\u2019s Legal Adviser Attorney-at-Law J. M. Wijebandara, BASL President Attorney-at-Law Rajeev Amarasuriya and senior BASL representatives attended the meeting."
