    "chunk_id": "2026-08-13-dailymirrorlk-9961b27c-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "bc020b505efa19946d4728701c817f2a",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2015,
    "chunk_text": "HNB Finance secures CRIB Silver for disciplined credit data governance\n\nHNB Finance PLC has secured the Silver Award in the Data Submission Volume, Category 4 at the CRIB Data Management and Compliance Awards 2026, organised by the Credit Information Bureau of Sri Lanka.\n\nThe recognition was presented at CRIB\u2019s Annual CEOs Forum and Institutional Rating Awards Ceremony 2026, which brought together leaders from Sri Lanka\u2019s banking and non-bank financial institution sectors to recognise excellence in credit-data management, institutional compliance and responsible financial practices.\n\nThe CRIB awards recognise financial institutions across key areas includingData Validity, Data Management Efficiency and Data Submission Volume, with Gold, Silver and Bronze honours presented within categories structured according to the scale and volume of information submitted by participating institutions.\n\nHNB Finance\u2019s Silver Award reflects the Company\u2019s continued commitment to submitting accurate, complete and timely credit information while maintaining the systems, controls and governance standards required managing customer data responsibly.\n\nThe awards follow a stringent institution-level assessment process covering the validity, accuracy, consistency, completeness and timeliness of credit information submitted to CRIB. Institutions are also assessed on data-management efficiency and adherence to applicable reporting, regulatory and compliance requirements.\n\nCommenting on the achievement, HNB Finance Managing Director, CEO Chaminda Prabhath said, \u201cAccurate and timely credit information is not simply a regulatory requirement. It directly affects the ability of customers to access finance and the quality of the lending decisions made by financial institutions. When customer credit records are maintained correctly, responsible borrowers can be assessed more fairly, lending decisions can be made more efficiently and unnecessary delays in obtaining financial facilities can be reduced.\u201d"
  },
