    "language": "en",
    "md5": "c21ea118c729c9509b0d1ca91744f74f",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1704,
    "chunk_text": "Commenting on the achievement, HNB Finance Managing Director, CEO Chaminda Prabhath said, \u201cAccurate and timely credit information is not simply a regulatory requirement. It directly affects the ability of customers to access finance and the quality of the lending decisions made by financial institutions. When customer credit records are maintained correctly, responsible borrowers can be assessed more fairly, lending decisions can be made more efficiently and unnecessary delays in obtaining financial facilities can be reduced.\u201d\n\nReliable credit information has become increasingly important as Sri Lanka seeks to expand access to formal finance while strengthening financial-sector stability. Accurate credit records help reduce information gaps between borrowers and lenders, support objective credit assessments and enable financial institutions to extend credit more responsibly.\n\nFor customers, improved credit-data quality can contribute to faster assessments, more transparent lending decisions and better access to appropriately structured financial products. At the institutional level, it strengthens credit-risk management, responsible lending and the early identification of potential repayment risks.\n\nHNB Finance said the award would further encourage the Company to strengthen its data-governance systems, regulatory compliance framework, digital reporting capabilities and customer-information management practices.\n\nOrganised by Sri Lanka\u2019s statutory credit-information authority, the CRIB Institutional Rating Awards are regarded as among the country\u2019s most coveted recognitions for excellence in credit-data management and compliance within the financial-services industry."
