    "chunk_text": "Screenline Kandy ISO certification advances standards-led apparel manufacturing\n\nSri Lanka\u2019s Screenline (Private) Limited has secured ISO 9001:2015 certification for its Kandy manufacturing facility, marking a further step in strengthening the company\u2019s quality-management systems and its alignment with international manufacturing standards required by increasingly demanding global apparel supply chains.\n\nLocated at Lot 4/A, Kandy Industrial Park, BOI Kengalla, the facility has been officially certified by SGS United Kingdom Ltd for its management system covering the manufacture of heat-seal labels and graphics and the provision of thermal pressing services.\n\nThe certification further strengthens Screenline\u2019s position as a Sri Lankan manufacturer of heat-seal and thermal-transfer solutions serving the international apparel industry, at a time when global buyers are placing greater emphasis on quality consistency, traceability, product safety, environmental accountability and adherence to internationally recognised production standards.\n\nCommenting on the achievement, Screenline Managing Director Nishantha Bakmeege said the certification represented an important step in strengthening both the company\u2019s manufacturing systems and its ability to compete in international markets.\n\n\u201cISO 9001:2015 certification is an important recognition of the systems, processes and quality discipline we have built into our Kandy manufacturing operation. For us, this is not simply about obtaining an international certification; it is about creating greater consistency, strengthening customer confidence and ensuring that our manufacturing capabilities continue to meet the expectations of global apparel supply chains. As we expand our presence in international markets, maintaining recognised standards in quality, product safety and responsible manufacturing will remain central to our business strategy,\u201d Bakmeege said."
  },
