    "chunk_text": "\u201cISO 9001:2015 certification is an important recognition of the systems, processes and quality discipline we have built into our Kandy manufacturing operation. For us, this is not simply about obtaining an international certification; it is about creating greater consistency, strengthening customer confidence and ensuring that our manufacturing capabilities continue to meet the expectations of global apparel supply chains. As we expand our presence in international markets, maintaining recognised standards in quality, product safety and responsible manufacturing will remain central to our business strategy,\u201d Bakmeege said.\n\nScreenline\u2019s heat-seal products are currently supplied to international markets including Mexico, Ghana, Bangladesh, Vietnam and Pakistan, linking the company\u2019s Sri Lankan manufacturing capabilities with customers across a diverse range of global apparel markets.\n\nThe Kandy facility forms an important part of this expanding manufacturing capability, with the new ISO certification reinforcing Screenline\u2019s focus on delivering products that meet consistent quality requirements and international customer expectations.\n\nThe achievement also highlights the wider importance of standards-led manufacturing as Sri Lankan exporters seek to strengthen their position within global value chains. Internationally recognised quality-management systems can play an increasingly important role in supporting market access, building buyer confidence and enabling local manufacturers to compete on quality, reliability and compliance rather than cost alone.\n\nThe company also holds OEKO-TEX STANDARD 100 certification covering a range of printed and heat-transfer applications, including heat seals and thermal transfers.\n\nImportantly, this certification is held under Product Class I \u2013 baby articles, reflecting the stringent requirements applicable to products intended for particularly sensitive uses."
