    "md5": "25c3df5f9b7344902407d35ed23e8c3f",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1627,
    "chunk_text": "Am\u00e3na Bank marks 15th anniversary with commemorative cover and stamp\n\nDeputy Postmaster General of the Sri Lanka Department of Posts, Premachandra Herath, hands over Am\u00e3na Bank\u2019s Special Commemorative Cover and Stamp to Chairman Asgi Akbarally, in the presence of Managing Director/CEO Mohamed Azmeer and Director of the Philatelic Bureau, Lanka De Silva\n\nAm\u00e3na Bank PLC in collaboration with the Philatelic Bureau of the Department of Posts of Sri Lanka launched a special commemorative cover and stamp in celebration of the Bank\u2019s 15th anniversary.\n\nThe ceremonial launch was held on 12 August to honour and mark Am\u00e3na Bank\u2019s contribution to Sri Lanka\u2019s financial services landscape and its distinctive role as the country\u2019s first and only licensed commercial bank operating entirely on the non-interest based banking model.\n\nThe commemorative cover and stamp pay tribute to Am\u00e3na Bank\u2019s journey since commencing operations in 2011, reflecting 15 years of enabling growth, enriching lives, and delivering value through a development-focused and people-friendly approach to banking.\n\nSince opening its doors, Am\u00e3na Bank has steadily expanded its presence across the country, serving a growing customer base through its 80+ branch and self-banking centre network while remaining focused on Retail, SME, and development-oriented banking with a selective approach to corporates. The Bank\u2019s asset-backed banking model continues to channel financing towards productive sectors of the economy, supporting entrepreneurs, households, and businesses in a manner aligned with its values and customer-centric promise."
  },
