    "chunk_text": "SHRM strengthens Sri Lanka presence\n\nThe Society for Human Resource Management (SHRM), the world\u2019s largest HR professional association, with close to 340,000 members across more than 180 countries, has strengthened its presence in Sri Lanka, with dedicated local leadership and an expanded range of services for the HR professionals and organisations.\n\nSHRM India and APAC Senior Director Consulting and BD Dedeepya (Dedu) Ajith John will lead SHRM\u2019s business in Sri Lanka, while the respected Sri Lankan HR leader and coach Oshana Dias has been appointed as SHRM Sri Lanka Country Lead.\n\nThey will be supported by SHRM Senior Consultant Kaavya Sasidharan, who will work closely with the team on consulting engagements.\n\nSHRM has maintained a presence in Sri Lanka through its relationship with the Association of Human Resource Professionals (AHRP). The strengthened direct presence marks the next phase of SHRM\u2019s engagement with the market, providing the HR professionals and organisations with greater access to its global expertise, professional development resources and organisational consulting capabilities.\n\nSHRM will continue to offer its memberships and globally recognised SHRM-CP (Certified Professional) and SHRM-SCP (Senior Certified Professional) certifications, while expanding access to consulting and capability-building solutions.\n\nIts consulting portfolio covers organisational design, talent management, leadership development, workforce planning, HR transformation, research and assessment centres, supporting organisations in addressing broader workforce and organisational priorities.\n\nThe Sri Lankan HR professionals will also have access to a special SHRM membership rate of US $ 49 for a limited period. The membership provides access to SHRM\u2019s global research, toolkits and templates, its Ask an Advisor service, discounted certification and event rates and connections with SHRM\u2019s international professional community."
  },
