    "md5": "f150ad75246b5f257fcd7a668c1f86af",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1842,
    "chunk_text": "The Sri Lankan HR professionals will also have access to a special SHRM membership rate of US $ 49 for a limited period. The membership provides access to SHRM\u2019s global research, toolkits and templates, its Ask an Advisor service, discounted certification and event rates and connections with SHRM\u2019s international professional community.\n\nSHRM also plans to introduce master classes tailored to the Sri Lankan market, combining its global research and body of knowledge with practical learning for local practitioners.\n\nThe expanded presence will also create greater regional opportunities for Sri Lankan HR and business leaders. The 15th SHRM HR Excellence Awards, held as part of the SHRM India Annual Conference, are now open to Sri Lankan organisations and HR professionals.\n\nThe Sri Lankan delegates will also receive preferential access to SHRM Annual Conferences in India, MENA and the United States, including a special delegate rate of US $ 215 for the SHRM India Annual Conference and Expo on November 26 and 27, 2026, in New Delhi.\n\nThe organisations will additionally be able to access SHRM\u2019s wider portfolio of research and thought leadership, assessment centres, corporate training and academies, executive development and leadership programmes.\n\n\u201cSri Lanka has been an important market for SHRM over the years. During this time, we have had the privilege of working alongside AHRP, clients and HR leaders to strengthen the profession and build organisational capability.\n\nOshana\u2019s appointment as Country Lead is a natural next step in deepening that relationship. Through dedicated on-ground leadership, supported by Dedeepya and Kaavya, we aim to combine regional experience, local insight and SHRM\u2019s global capabilities to create greater impact for organisations and HR professionals in Sri Lanka,\u201d said Khanna."
  },
