    "md5": "7d7b0103aeb067ec354a095e0d54a736",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1882,
    "chunk_text": "Crescent recognised for purpose-driven storytelling at 31st Sumathi Awards\n\nFrom left: Lakmal Jayasekara - General Manager - Sales & Marketing, Norfolk Foods (Pvt.) Ltd.; Samurdhi Ranasinghe - Film Director; Kaushi Siriwardena \u2013 CEO, Watermark Adverts (Pvt.) Ltd.; Ameena Ziauddin - President/MD, Norfolk Foods (Pvt.) Ltd.; Milani Dias - Brand Manager, Norfolk Foods (Pvt.) Ltd.; and Esha Ushneesha Jayasinghe- Creative Officer/ Production Designer, Watermark Adverts (Pvt.) Ltd\n\nCrescent, the flagship retail brand of Norfolk Foods (Pvt) Ltd., has been recognised with the 2nd Runner-up award for Best Television Commercial at the 31st Sumathi Awards 2026.\n\nThe recognition, presented recently at the awards ceremony held at Monarch Imperial, marks an important milestone in Crescent\u2019s journey of creating campaigns that connect with consumers through authentic and relatable storytelling.\n\nFeaturing a departure from conventional representations of men in the household, the commercial tells the story of a husband who celebrates his wedding anniversary by lovingly preparing a meal for his wife and child. Through this simple yet powerful narrative, the campaign encourages a more inclusive perspective on family roles while demonstrating how expressions of love are best reflected in everyday acts of care.\n\nDeveloped in partnership with Watermark Adverts, the award also recognises the creative collaboration between Crescent and Watermark Adverts in bringing a campaign to life that reflects evolving family dynamics in Sri Lanka while celebrating love, family, and shared responsibility. By placing a husband and father at the centre of the kitchen, the commercial uses Crescent\u2019s distinctive range of effortless and straightforward meals to challenge long-held perceptions while reinforcing the importance of partnership, equality, and mutual appreciation in the home."
  },
