    "chunk_text": "SL poultry producers honoured as Global Sustainability Leaders at Soy Connext 2026\n\nSeen here are several poultry producers from Sri Lanka recognized as global sustainable leaders\n\nSri Lanka, 2025\u2019s largest market in the world for containerised US soybean meal, had its poultry sector honoured on the global stage recently, with several of the country\u2019s leading poultry producers and feed millers recognised among global sustainability leaders for their use of the Sustainable U.S. Soy and Fed with Sustainable U.S. Soy labels, at Soy Connext 2026, the flagship summit of the US Soybean Export Council (USSEC) in Chicago.\n\nThe recognition came during a dedicated sustainability session at Soy Connext, which brought together a record 800-plus delegates from around the world, the largest turnout in the event\u2019s history. Sri Lanka\u2019s poultry champions stood alongside honourees from the Americas, Greater China, and Southeast Asia, marking one of the strongest showings yet for South Asia at the event. Mark and Comm, the Colombo-based PR and communications agency, having worked closely with USSEC on Sri Lanka\u2019s soy sector messaging, attended the summit as a media delegate and was present for the recognition.\n\nThe three-day summit, held August 5 to 7 at the Hyatt Regency Chicago, opened with the Trade Team Invitational, a series of one on one meetings pairing international buyers with US exporters, before moving into a full agenda of keynotes and breakout sessions on global market dynamics, sustainability, and supply chain resilience."
