    "chunk_size_bytes": 1116,
    "chunk_text": "Cabinet approves coal supply contracts for Lakvijaya Power Plant\n\nTo supply coal to the Lakvijaya Power Plant in Norochcholai, the Cabinet of Ministers has approved the award of contracts to two companies, for the 2026/2027 period.\n\nThe approval follows a Cabinet decision on March 30, 2026, to procure 2.28 million metric tonnes of coal, with a \u00b110 percent variation, to meet the power plant\u2019s operational requirements.\n\nAccording to the Government Information Department, the decision to source coal from two suppliers was taken to minimise the risk of supply disruptions and ensure uninterrupted electricity generation and energy security.\n\nFollowing an international competitive bidding process, nine tenders were received and evaluated by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee.\n\nBased on the committee\u2019s recommendations, Aditya Birla Global Trading (Singapore) Pte. Ltd has been awarded 70 percent of the requirement, amounting to 1.596 million metric tonnes (\u00b110 percent), while India\u2019s Mohit Minerals Limited will supply the remaining 30 percent or 684,000 metric tonnes (\u00b110 percent)."
